{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Label Analyzer - CLP Compliance Checker\n",
    "\n",
    "Production-ready analyzer for product label compliance checking using Gemini 3 Pro.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What it does:**\n",
    "1. Calibrates DPI automatically from label\n",
    "2. Detects CLP (regulatory) vs non-CLP (marketing) sections\n",
    "3. **Measures** font size, line spacing, contrast (Gemini)\n",
    "4. **Validates** against compliance rules (deterministic, 100% reproducible)\n",
    "5. Flags uncertain results for human review\n",
    "\n",
    "**Output:** Structured compliance report with:\n",
    "- Measurement confidence (0-1)\n",
    "- Pass/Fail verdict for each rule\n",
    "- Human review flags for borderline cases"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install dependencies (run once)\n",
    "!pip install -q google-genai pillow pymupdf pydantic python-dotenv"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Import the analyzer\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import os\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add current directory to path (so we can import label_analyzer_production)\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, str(Path.cwd()))\n",
    "\n",
    "from label_analyzer_production import (\n",
    "    LabelAnalyzer,\n",
    "    PartClassification,\n",
    "    analyze_image_file\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "import json\n",
    "from IPython.display import JSON, Markdown, display\n",
    "from PIL import Image as PIL_Image\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ Imports successful\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Configuration\n",
    "PROJECT_ID = \"your-gcp-project-id\"  # Replace with your GCP project\n",
    "DPI = 300  # Default DPI (will be calibrated from label if measurement line found)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create data directories\n",
    "os.makedirs(\"data/in\", exist_ok=True)\n",
    "os.makedirs(\"data/out\", exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✅ Configuration ready\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Project ID: {PROJECT_ID}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Default DPI: {DPI}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Load Label Image"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Path to your label PDF or image\n",
    "# Place files in: ./data/in/\n",
    "IMAGE_PATH = \"data/in/your_label.pdf\"  # Change this to your file\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check if file exists\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(IMAGE_PATH):\n",
    "    print(f\"❌ File not found: {IMAGE_PATH}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n📁 Place your label PDF/image in: data/in/\")\n",
    "    print(f\"   Then update IMAGE_PATH above and re-run this cell\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"✅ File ready: {IMAGE_PATH}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load and display the image\n",
    "from label_analyzer_production import pdf_to_image\n",
    "\n",
    "if IMAGE_PATH.lower().endswith('.pdf'):\n",
    "    # Convert PDF to image\n",
    "    img = pdf_to_image(IMAGE_PATH, dpi=DPI)\n",
    "    print(f\"✅ PDF converted to image: {img.size[0]}×{img.size[1]} pixels\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    # Load image directly\n",
    "    img = PIL_Image.open(IMAGE_PATH)\n",
    "    print(f\"✅ Image loaded: {img.size[0]}×{img.size[1]} pixels\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display\n",
    "display(img.resize((img.width // 2, img.height // 2)))  # Show at 50% for readability"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Run Analysis Pipeline"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Authenticate with Google Cloud (required once per session)\n",
    "!gcloud auth application-default login"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialize analyzer\n",
    "from label_analyzer_production import image_to_base64\n",
    "\n",
    "analyzer = LabelAnalyzer(project_id=PROJECT_ID, dpi=DPI)\nprint(f\"✅ Analyzer initialized\")\nprint(f\"   DPI: {DPI}\")\nprint(f\"   Project: {PROJECT_ID}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code">
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Convert image to base64 for Gemini\n",
    "image_data = image_to_base64(img)\n",
    "print(f\"✅ Image encoded for Gemini API\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Run full analysis pipeline\n",
    "# This takes ~30-60 seconds per image\n",
    "print(\"⏳ Running analysis (this takes ~30-60 seconds)...\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "detected_parts = analyzer.analyze(img, image_data)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n✅ Analysis complete: {len(detected_parts)} regions detected\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: Results Summary"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Summary table\n",
    "print(\"\\n📊 DETECTION SUMMARY\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "print(f\"{'Classification':<12} {'Label':<30} {'Confidence':<12} {'Compliant':<10}\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 80)\n",
    "\n",
    "clp_count = 0\n",
    "compliant_count = 0\n",
    "review_count = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "for part in detected_parts:\n",
    "    if part.classification == PartClassification.CLP:\n",
    "        clp_count += 1\n",
    "        is_compliant = part.is_compliant()\n",
    "        needs_review = part.needs_human_review()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        if is_compliant:\n",
    "            compliant_count += 1\n",
    "        if needs_review:\n",
    "            review_count += 1\n",
    "        \n",
    "        status = \"PASS ✓\" if is_compliant else \"FAIL ✗\"\n",
    "        if needs_review:\n",
    "            status += \" (REVIEW)\"\n",
    "        \n",
    "        confidence = part.compliance_check.get('measurement_confidence', 0) if part.compliance_check else 0\n",
    "        print(f\"{part.classification.value:<12} {part.label:<30} {confidence:.0%}         {status:<10}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 80)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nCLP REGIONS: {clp_count} total\")\n",
    "print(f\"  ✓ Compliant: {compliant_count}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  ✗ Non-compliant: {clp_count - compliant_count}\")\n",
    "if review_count > 0:\n",
    "    print(f\"  ⚠️  Needs review: {review_count} (uncertain or borderline)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4: Detailed Rule Breakdown"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Show detailed compliance results for each CLP region\n",
    "for i, part in enumerate(detected_parts, 1):\n",
    "    if part.classification != PartClassification.CLP:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"\\n{'=' * 80}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"CLP Region {i}: {part.label}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"{'=' * 80}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if not part.compliance_check:\n",
    "        print(\"(No compliance data)\")\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Measurements\n",
    "    measurements = part.compliance_check.get('measurements', {})\n",
    "    if measurements:\n",
    "        print(f\"\\n📏 MEASUREMENTS (Gemini)\")\n",
    "        print(f\"  Font size: {measurements.get('font_size_mm', 'N/A'):.2f} mm ({measurements.get('font_size_pixels', 'N/A'):.0f} px)\")\n",
    "        print(f\"  Line distance: {measurements.get('line_distance_mm', 'N/A'):.2f} mm ({measurements.get('line_distance_pixels', 'N/A'):.0f} px)\")\n",
    "        print(f\"  Background: {measurements.get('background_color')} | Text: {measurements.get('text_color')}\")\n",
    "        print(f\"  Contrast: {measurements.get('contrast_assessment')}\")\n",
    "        print(f\"  Confidence: {measurements.get('measurement_confidence', 0):.0%}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Rule results\n",
    "    rule_results = part.compliance_check.get('rule_results', {})\n",
    "    if rule_results:\n",
    "        print(f\"\\n✓/✗ COMPLIANCE RULES\")\n",
    "        \n",
    "        rule_1 = rule_results.get('rule_1_font_size', {})\n",
    "        print(f\"  1. Font Size: {rule_1.get('status')}\")\n",
    "        print(f\"     {rule_1.get('detail')}\")\n",
    "        \n",
    "        rule_2 = rule_results.get('rule_2_line_distance', {})\n",
    "        print(f\"  2. Line Distance: {rule_2.get('status')}\")\n",
    "        print(f\"     {rule_2.get('detail')}\")\n",
    "        \n",
    "        rule_3 = rule_results.get('rule_3_background_contrast', {})\n",
    "        print(f\"  3. Contrast: {rule_3.get('status')}\")\n",
    "        print(f\"     {rule_3.get('detail')}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Overall verdict\n",
    "    overall = part.compliance_check.get('overall_compliance', 'UNKNOWN')\n",
    "    needs_review = part.needs_human_review()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"\\n{'🎯 VERDICT':-^80}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Overall: {overall}\")\n",
    "    if needs_review:\n",
    "        print(f\"  ⚠️  HUMAN REVIEW NEEDED (uncertain or borderline)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5: Visualize Detections"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize detected regions on the image\n",
    "visualized = analyzer.visualize(img)\n",
    "display(visualized.resize((visualized.width // 2, visualized.height // 2)))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save visualization\n",
    "output_path = \"data/out/labeled_analysis.jpg\"\n",
    "visualized.save(output_path)\n",
    "print(f\"✅ Visualization saved: {output_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6: Export Results"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Export full results to JSON for programmatic use\n",
    "import json\n",
    "from datetime import datetime\n",
    "\n",
    "output_data = {\n",
    "    \"timestamp\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n",
    "    \"image_file\": IMAGE_PATH,\n",
    "    \"summary\": {\n",
    "        \"total_regions\": len(detected_parts),\n",
    "        \"clp_regions\": sum(1 for p in detected_parts if p.classification == PartClassification.CLP),\n",
    "        \"compliant_regions\": sum(1 for p in detected_parts if p.is_compliant()),\n",
    "        \"review_needed\": sum(1 for p in detected_parts if p.needs_human_review())\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"regions\": []\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "for part in detected_parts:\n",
    "    region_data = {\n",
    "        \"classification\": part.classification.value,\n",
    "        \"label\": part.label,\n",
    "        \"content_type\": part.content_type,\n",
    "        \"confidence\": part.confidence,\n",
    "        \"bounds\": {\n",
    "            \"xmin\": part.rect.xmin,\n",
    "            \"ymin\": part.rect.ymin,\n",
    "            \"xmax\": part.rect.xmax,\n",
    "            \"ymax\": part.rect.ymax\n",
    "        },\n",
    "        \"is_compliant\": part.is_compliant(),\n",
    "        \"needs_review\": part.needs_human_review(),\n",
    "        \"compliance_check\": part.compliance_check\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    output_data[\"regions\"].append(region_data)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save to file\n",
    "output_json = \"data/out/compliance_report.json\"\n",
    "with open(output_json, 'w') as f:\n",
    "    json.dump(output_data, f, indent=2)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✅ Results exported: {output_json}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📋 Summary:\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Total regions: {output_data['summary']['total_regions']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   CLP regions: {output_data['summary']['clp_regions']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Compliant: {output_data['summary']['compliant_regions']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Needs review: {output_data['summary']['review_needed']}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Next Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "✅ **Analysis complete!**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Output files saved to `data/out/`:**\n",
    "- `compliance_report.json` - Full compliance data (for portfolio updates)\n",
    "- `labeled_analysis.jpg` - Visualization of detected regions\n",
    "\n",
    "**For batch processing multiple labels:**\n",
    "```python\n",
    "from label_analyzer_production import analyze_batch\n",
    "\n",
    "results = analyze_batch(\n",
    "    image_paths=[\"data/in/label1.pdf\", \"data/in/label2.pdf\"],\n",
    "    project_id=PROJECT_ID,\n",
    "    dpi=DPI,\n",
    "    max_workers=3  # Concurrent processing\n",
    ")\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key insights:**\n",
    "- ✓ Two-layer validation (Gemini measures → local rules apply)\n",
    "- ✓ 100% deterministic rule checking (same input = same output)\n",
    "- ⚠️ Uncertain results flagged for human review\n",
    "- 📊 Structured JSON output ready for database/spreadsheet import"
   ]
  }
